  "notes": "{見出|みいだ}す is a transitive godan verb. It has a somewhat literary and formal tone compared to {見|み}つける.\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{見出|みいだ}している indicates a state of having discovered something.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- Xを{見出|みいだ}す (discover X)\n- Xに{意味|いみ}を{見出|みいだ}す (find meaning in X)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {才能|さいのう}を{見出|みいだ}す (discover talent)\n- {意味|いみ}を{見出|みいだ}す (find meaning)\n- {価値|かち}を{見出|みいだ}す (find value)\n- {解決策|かいけつさく}を{見出|みいだ}す (find a solution)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {見出|みいだ}す vs {見|み}つける: {見出|みいだ}す is more literary and implies deeper discovery or recognition of value, while {見|み}つける is more everyday and means simply finding something.",
